r value for an error."],[1791,"Stdout Sink"],[1812,"Storage Backends"],[1152,"Storage Engine"],[1859,"Storage Full: Implement state cleanup policies"],[1852,"Storage Location: Use persistent storage locations for production deployments"],[1864,"Storage usage for state files"],[130,"Store consumer offset"],[856,"Store consumer offset"],[1640,"store_access_key_id: The access key ID of the object storage."],[1643,"store_class: The storage class to use. Currently, only S3-compatible storage is supported."],[129,"store_consumer_offset"],[1642,"store_region: The region of the object storage, if applicable."],[1641,"store_secret_access_key: The secret key used to upload data to the object storage."],[1639,"store_url: The URL of the object storage for data uploads."],[927,"stored_offset - 8 bytes"],[2365,"StoreOffsetAsync(offset, partitionId, resetLastPolled = false) stores the offset for a partition; pass resetLastPolled: true to also move the consumer's cached last-polled position so the next poll resumes past the stored offset. DeleteOffsetAsync(partitionId) clears the stored offset."],[599,"Strategy"],[612,"Strategy"],[1216,"Strategy"],[997,"strategy - 9 bytes (1 byte kind + 8 bytes u64 value)"],[1575,"strategy - the way in which we want to poll the messages. The default one being Offset (underlying PollingKind enum) means that we will start polling the messages from the particular offset provided in the value field - it's on the client, to keep track of the most recent offset. On the other hand, we could also use the different kind, for example Next, which means, that the next messages will be returned to the client, depending on the so-called consumer offset value stored on the server side. The client may not need to track the offset on its own anymore, but instead, call store_offset() to save it on the server (e.g. after each processed message or the whole batch), or make use of  auto_commit: true, to automatically commit the offset on the server side, once the messages are fetched (this one results in the so called at-most-once delivery mode)."],[1413,"Stream"],[2553,"Stream Builder"],[2486,"Stream builder - examples using the IggyStream, IggyStreamProducer, and IggyStreamConsumer builder APIs as discussed in the stream builder guide."],[464,"Stream management"],[1110,"Stream permissions"],[1126,"Stream permissions - per-stream operations (manage stream, read stream, manage topics, read topics, poll messages, send messages)"],[1571,"stream_id - the ID of the stream (numeric or string) from which we want to poll the messages."],[937,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[943,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[945,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[949,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[951,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[954,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[956,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[965,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[968,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[977,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[980,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[984,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[988,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[994,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1001,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1006,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1012,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1017,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1023,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1027,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1031,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1034,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1039,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1043,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[1047,"stream_id - variable (Identifier)"],[2436,"stream-builder - stream builder API usage"],[2447,"stream-builder - stream builder API usage"],[2464,"stream-builder - stream builder API usage"],[2417,"streambuilder - combined producer and consumer in one class"],[589,"StreamClient - create, get, list, update, delete, purge streams"],[41,"Streams"],[831,"Streams"],[2018,"Streams"],[1288,"Streams - list, c